cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "drt-mixed-hailing-model: analytical model of demand-responsive transit with mixed hailing and a heterogeneous fleet"
version: 1.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Steady-state workload-state queueing model of pooling-enabled demand-responsive transit serving
  e-hail and street-hail users with autonomous vehicles (e-hail only) and human-driven vehicles
  (both modes), with patience limits, and scripts that reproduce the figures and tables of the paper.
keywords:
  - demand-responsive transit
  - ride-pooling
  - street-hailing
  - autonomous vehicles
  - queueing network
authors:
  - given-names: Hyuncheol
    family-names: Park
    affiliation: Korea University
  - given-names: Seungmo
    family-names: Kang
    affiliation: Korea University
